  "notes": "A mature Norway spruce, low-poly but faithful: 30 m tall with a 7.6-13.7 m spread and a 1-1.5 m bole (Morton Arboretum / conifers.org; the species reaches 35-55 m). ★ THE BOLE IS SIX STACKED CYLINDERS OF DECREASING RADIUS, not one — a constant-radius cylinder is not a trunk, and modelling 30 m of bole as one gave 9.5 tonnes against a real Norway spruce's 3-6. The fix is the taper, NOT a smaller radius chosen to land on a nicer number: the geometry was wrong, so the geometry is what changed. The crown is FIVE STACKED WHORLS of decreasing radius rather than a sphere, because a spruce is a cone and the taper is the tree's actual shape — the cheapest geometry that is still the right geometry. Crown packing = LAI x needle thickness / crown depth = 6.0 x 0.50 mm / 20.0 m = 1.50e-04. ★ It is EVERGREEN, and that is not a property written here — it follows from `conifer_foliage` carrying no senescent spectrum. The same time signal that turns the oak leaves this one alone.",
